                    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
                    "body": "> I used to use 'coc.nvim' for a brief time, but switched to built-in diagnostics. Which seems also to be a better overall approach for 'mini.nvim'.\r\n\r\nI don't really have a strong opinion on this; both options are excellent. :)\r\n\r\nPersonally, I've grown to trust @fannheyward and the community for their excellent work on CoC, which addresses a much broader range of needs beyond *\"just\"* LSP alone. \r\n\r\n> Also, there doesn't seem to be a reason to override gen_ai_spec.diagnostic for this to be used in the 'mini.ai' spec. A less nested coc_diagnostic_spec = function(ai_type) ... end should be enough.\r\n\r\nCorrect! \r\n\r\nI chose to do it that way in my own setup to maintain coherence in my configuration. My approach isn't a strict requirement, of course. 🍻",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I used to use 'coc.nvim' for a brief time, but switched to built-in diagnostics. Which seems also to be a better overall approach for 'mini.nvim'.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I don't really have a strong opinion on this; both options are excellent. :)</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Personally, I've grown to trust <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/fannheyward/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/fannheyward\">@fannheyward</a> and the community for their excellent work on CoC, which addresses a much broader range of needs beyond <em>\"just\"</em> LSP alone.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also, there doesn't seem to be a reason to override gen_ai_spec.diagnostic for this to be used in the 'mini.ai' spec. A less nested coc_diagnostic_spec = function(ai_type) ... end should be enough.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Correct!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I chose to do it that way in my own setup to maintain coherence in my configuration. My approach isn't a strict requirement, of course. 🍻</p>",
                    "bodyText": "I used to use 'coc.nvim' for a brief time, but switched to built-in diagnostics. Which seems also to be a better overall approach for 'mini.nvim'.\n\nI don't really have a strong opinion on this; both options are excellent. :)\nPersonally, I've grown to trust @fannheyward and the community for their excellent work on CoC, which addresses a much broader range of needs beyond \"just\" LSP alone.\n\nAlso, there doesn't seem to be a reason to override gen_ai_spec.diagnostic for this to be used in the 'mini.ai' spec. A less nested coc_diagnostic_spec = function(ai_type) ... end should be enough.\n\nCorrect!\nI chose to do it that way in my own setup to maintain coherence in my configuration. My approach isn't a strict requirement, of course. 🍻",
